adjudication.rationale:
In `store.js.es6` the new plural branch matches keys like `foo_ids` and does:

```js
const hydrated = obj[k].map(id => self._lookupSubType(subType, type, id, root));
obj[self.pluralize(subType)] = hydrated || [];
delete obj[k];
```

This is a verifiable behavior change vs the singular `_id` case: it deletes the original `*_ids` field unconditionally, even if `_lookupSubType` can’t resolve any of the ids (e.g., when the sideloaded collection for that subtype is absent). That can yield arrays containing `undefined` entries and, importantly, it discards the original ids so the client can’t later distinguish “unhydrated/missing sideloaded data” from a real hydration result based on ids. Also, `hydrated || []` is indeed dead code because `.map(...)` always returns an array (truthy), even when empty.
